# kc2mm:ignore
menu "Network"

config LWIP
    bool "lwIP TCP/IP stack"
    default n
    help
      lwIP 2.x (BSD) with IPv4, TCP, UDP, DHCP and DNS. Link-agnostic:
      WIFI_LWIP (the on-chip radio) and USB_NET (USB ethernet, iPhone
      tethering) each add a network interface on top of it.

config USB_NET
    bool "USB network link (iPhone tethering)"
    depends on USB_HOST
    select LWIP
    default n
    help
      Drives Apple's USB tethering interface (iPhone with Personal
      Hotspot on, behind the OTG hub) as an lwIP interface. Holds the
      OTG port in host mode while enabled, so USB-MIDI to a computer is
      off at the same time. Needs no radio: coexists with BLE.

config USB_NET_AUTO
    bool "Hold the USB port in host mode for the network link from boot"
    depends on USB_NET || USB_NET_ECM
    default n
    help
      Starts with "USB NET" and "USB ETH" on: the OTG port goes to host mode as
      soon as no computer is driving it, and whichever network link is plugged
      in (a phone, a CDC-ECM adapter) comes up without a visit to the settings menu. Meant for a unit that lives on its hub with a phone,
      and for the emulator (fm1-live --usb ethernet): with it, the FM-1 is never
      a USB-MIDI device to a computer.

config USB_NET_ECM
    bool "USB CDC-ECM ethernet adapter"
    depends on USB_HOST
    select LWIP
    default n
    help
      CDC-ECM host driver for standard USB Ethernet adapters (e.g.
      ASIX AX88179A). Devices that expose a CDC-ECM configuration
      are switched to it automatically. Shares the OTG port and
      .pool_net RAM with USB_NET (iPhone tethering).

endmenu
